Lots of criticism here, but I like the idea and I'm offering some 
suggestions on the implementation too.

The scope of this class is probably WAY too much to implement, and it's 
CERTAINLY too much for plain ol' vanilla. Think about it: Not only a new 
class, but an entirely new set of equipment for it to start with. Even a 
new /category/ of weapons you're talking about. You'd have to set what 
other classes could advance in Firearms.

An entirely new game mechanic is introduced in the 'reloading' part, 
though I guess they could be some sort of container that only holds 
ammo.. but then clips? It's very complex.

Headshots I guess are handled like Vorpal Blade (which is NOT like you 
said, based off dex and skill), but sure seem out of place. More likely 
if you're stuck on head shots you could have it do bonus damage like the 
d20 silver damage. It's hard to imagine a headshot with a pistol doing 
much to a mastodon, and it's hard to imagine shooting a newt in the head.

I assume the functionality of 'Reason' is taken from the book which I've 
not yet read. I don't know how you'd make armor useless against it, 
since armor reduces your chance of being hit with a wounding blow. If 
you want to make it armor piercing, I think just increasing the damage 
is a closer approximation. It sounds like it would make a good quest 
artifact, and maybe #invoking it provides you some ammo much like the 
Longbow.

Sniper rifles would probably merit their own weapon category. After 
firing, you should be paralyzed for a turn or more to simulate the time 
it takes to fire. Tranqs are an interesting idea but I don't see the 
point if you don't also remove wands of sleep (or make gunslingers 
incapable of using (most) wands, which might offset some of how 
overpowered this sounds).

In all, it'd be a friggin HUGE patch, but it would be pretty cool if 
done right. So, I guess you'd better get programming...

